  "query_preview": "..\nShowers are expected to become scattered with isolated thunderstorms\ntonight. Shower coverage may increase by morning for Guam and Rota \nwith locally heavy showers possible. Meanwhile, Tinian and Saipan \nlook to have isolated showers in the morning, with scattered island \neffect showers possible and drifting east or northeast. The gradient \nof higher moisture over Guam and Rota will likely remain Thursday \nnight before pushing north Friday and bringing the potential for \nscattered, locally heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms to all \nislands. Winds will also likely increase to gentle to moderate as the\nmonsoon flow shifts north. This wet pattern may continue into the \nweekend and next week depending on the track and intensity of nearby \nInvest 90W. This will be monitored closely throughout the next week.",
